# foreman-kit loads ./.env from the directory it runs in (variables already set
# in the environment win). Copy this file to .env and fill in what you need.
# See README.md -> "Environment Variables (.env)".
#
# No variable changes a setting: the settings are in .foreman-kit/*.yaml, and a value
# for one run is `foreman-kit --set <file>.<key>=<value> <command>`. This file
# holds the secrets.

# --- The evaluator (gate evaluation; today the Jev model) ---------------------
# One API key is required (or a ~/.config/jev/credentials.json file).
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# --- The diagnostics assistant (optional, off as shipped) ----------------------
# Turn it on and choose its provider in .foreman-kit/pipeline.yaml (diagnostics:).
# Keep comments on their own line: an empty value followed by "# ..." would be
# read as the value itself.
# The kit's own name for the key, checked first; the only key variable for compat.
# FOREMANKIT_DIAGNOSTICS_API_KEY=

# The provider's own variable (used when FOREMANKIT_DIAGNOSTICS_API_KEY is empty)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
